{
  "ablation": {
    "id": "A6",
    "configuration": "Learned lesion segmentation + ICDR rules only, no CNN",
    "establishes": "The interpretable baseline with a trained lesion channel. Paired with A3, which uses the classical candidate detector, it measures what Track B adds to the evidence channel. A3 measured 0.0000 sensitivity because counting microaneurysms can never satisfy an ICDR criterion above Level 1.",
    "uses_cnn": false,
    "source": "docs/SIH26038_design.html \u00a711.6",
    "note": "Identical to A3 in every respect except which lesion channel supplies the ICDR evidence, so the pair isolates the contribution of the trained segmentation network over the classical candidate detector. Inherits preprocessing, grading, data and operating_point from config/default.json."
